<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9987" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">condemnātor</span></b> ,
		ōris, m.
		id.. *<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>One who gives sentence, a condemner</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">delicti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Marc. 2, 9</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>One who causes a condemnation, an accuser</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Claudiae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					4, 66</span></i>
			; cf. condemno, II.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
